        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design (§4.3)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the water-level sensing that is actually wired and actually used by firmware is an HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor read on two ESP32 GPIOs (§1/§4.4)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, 'WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES' block: PR1 'LiDAR' SDA/SCL pins connect via H1 (PB_1.25mm) to global labels I2C_SDA / I2C_SCL; PR1 carries no DNP cross; no ultrasonic/HC-SR04 symbol present"}
      ],
      "impact": "This build substitutes the LiDAR rangefinder (wired onto the main I2C bus) for the intended ultrasonic HC-SR04 water-level sensor, which is absent. Because the firmware has no TF-Luna/uart block and no ultrasonic hardware is present, automatic top-off / reservoir-level sensing does not operate as specified; additionally an unaddressed I2C device is now loaded on the shared bus.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic wires the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR1) onto the I2C bus via H1 and omits the intended HC-SR04 ultrasonic water-level sensor, directly contradicting the specification's explicit statement that PR1 is excluded/unwired and that level sensing is done by an ultrasonic module on two GPIOs; this is a behavioural deviation in the water-level/ATO subsystem."
}

